       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. A confirmation alone doesn't change the safety problem. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum labeled dose of 200 mg. It has no recognized therapeutic use and carries a serious risk of harm. This patient has normal kidney and liver function and no other factors that would justify it.\n\nHere are some ways I can still help:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** Tell me the dose, such as 50 mg or 100 mg once daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Get a second opinion.** If you think there's a reason for supratherapeutic dosing, please discuss it with your attending and pharmacy first. Once they approve, I can enter the order with a note documenting the rationale and who approved it.\n- **Check for a different intent.** If this is meant to be a total dose over several days, or a different drug, tell me and I'll correct it.\n\nIf the patient may have taken an overdose, that needs urgent evaluation. Contact poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) or toxicology."
